# Musician Expense Tracker — Cursor Rules

Concise conventions loaded on every code edit. The full reference,
architecture diagrams, contracts, and incident history live in **AGENTS.md**.
Always read AGENTS.md before making non-trivial architectural changes.

## Project Overview
Discord bot for a musician/music teacher to track income & expenses via
photos, text, and audio. Uses Gemini 3 Flash for extraction, Google Sheets
for storage, SQLite (aiosqlite) for persistent state. High-confidence entries
auto-save; low-confidence prompt for clarification. Corrections are
field-level updates, not full re-extraction. Bot deployed on Fly.io
(`shared-cpu-1x:512mb`) with a persistent volume for SQLite at `/data`.

## File Responsibilities
- `main.py` — Thin Discord event dispatcher. Owns emoji reactions,
  attachment download, thread creation, mention resolution, retry/delete
  orchestrators. Delegates extraction logic to entry_manager.
- `entry_manager.py` — Entry lifecycle. Creates entries, processes
  corrections, runs dedupe, classifies retry/delete intent, coordinates
  db + gemini + sheets.
- `gemini_processor.py` — Gemini API. Transcribe audio, describe images,
  extract financial data, process corrections. Image resize (Pillow with
  `draft()` mode). Retry + 90s timeout wrapping.
- `sheets_manager.py` — Google Sheets CRUD via `gspread`. All public
  functions accept `tab_name`. Sync library, wrap in `asyncio.to_thread()`.
- `db.py` — SQLite via `aiosqlite`. Three tables: conversations (state +
  tab_name + user_id), media_cache, conversation_messages.
- `prompts.py` — System prompts AND Pydantic models. Tightly coupled —
  change them together.
- `config.py` — Env vars, logging setup, channel→tab map.

## Spreadsheet Schema
Columns: Date, Type, Category, Client/Event, Vendor, Mode of Payment,
Amount ($), Description, Notes, Discord Link, Timestamp.

Categories:
- Income: Teaching, Performance
- Expense: IT, Performance, Teaching

Client/Event and Mode of Payment are income-only. Vendor is expense-only.

## Coding Conventions
- Python 3.11+ with type hints on all function signatures.
- Async/await for all I/O. The Discord bot loop is async.
- `logging` with structured context: `thread=X op=Y | message`. Log
  elapsed time for Gemini calls and sheet ops.
- Catch exceptions in Discord event handlers — never crash the loop.
  Report errors to the user in the thread.
- Imports: stdlib → third-party → local.

## Key Libraries
- `discord.py` — Use `commands.Bot`, not raw `Client`.
- `google-genai` — Use `client.aio.models.generate_content()` for async.
  `types.Part.from_bytes()` for inline image/audio. `response_schema=Model`
  for structured JSON. NOT `google-generativeai` (different package).
- `gspread` — Synchronous; always wrap in `asyncio.to_thread()`.
- `aiosqlite` — Async SQLite for db.py.
- `Pillow` — Image resize; CPU-bound, also wrap in `asyncio.to_thread()`.

## Emoji Reactions
- ⏳ Processing
- ✅ Saved to sheet (or reply acknowledged)
- 💬 Waiting for user input
- ❌ Caught error
- ❓ No extractable content
- 🗑️ Entries deleted by user

Use `main.set_reaction(message, emoji)` — it blind-removes all known bot
reactions before adding the new one (don't trust `message.reactions` cache;
it can be stale during long-running operations).

## Critical Design Rules

### Corrections and saves
- Corrections use **field-level updates** (FollowupResult with FieldUpdate
  list), NOT full re-extraction. Never re-evaluate fields the user didn't
  mention.
- For already-saved entries, **always mirror field changes to the sheet
  immediately** via `update_entry_in_place`, even if Gemini also asked a
  follow-up question. Otherwise SQLite drifts from the sheet (2026-05-06
  incident).
- Never delete sheet rows before new rows are written. Use update-in-place
  for same-count corrections, safe-replace (write-then-delete) for count
  changes.
- Drop unparseable `amount` field_updates with a WARNING log; NEVER store
  `""` or other unparseable values (2026-05-07 incident).

### State
- All conversation state lives in SQLite. No in-memory dicts. Bot restarts
  are instant — no reconstruction needed.
- `conversations.user_id` is the original poster, used for @-mentions. Use
  `main._resolve_user_id(conv, thread)` so legacy rows with NULL user_id
  fall back to fetching the parent message's author and backfilling.
- Audio is transcribed once and cached in `media_cache`. Never re-send raw
  audio bytes to Gemini after the initial transcription.

### Destructive actions
- Retry-on-saved and delete-on-saved require an explicit confirmation via
  a `pending_*_confirm` gate. Use `entry_manager._is_affirmative(text)`
  for the confirmation check — it accepts `yes`, `yes!`, `Yes.`,
  `yes please`, `yep`, etc.
- The destructive-confirm prompts must @-mention the user — they touch
  data and missing them is high-cost.

### Memory safety (512mb VM)
- Always preprocess images upfront via `gemini_processor.preprocess_images`
  before the describe/extract phase; then `images.clear()` + `gc.collect()`
  to free originals.
- `PROCESSING_LOCK = asyncio.Semaphore(1)` wraps both message handlers —
  burst posts queue rather than running in parallel.
- Wrap every `generate_content` call in `asyncio.wait_for(..., 90)`.

### Dedupe
- An entry is a duplicate only when: amount equal within $0.01 AND date
  **exactly** equal (no fuzziness) AND a client OR vendor name match
  (substring). Do NOT match on type+category alone.
- Bias: false negative (extra row to delete) > false positive (silently
  dropped tax record).

### Mentions
- `_with_mention_if_needed(text, user_id, status)` for normal output.
- Always-mention prompts: retry-confirm, delete-confirm, recovery reposts,
  errors.

## Important Reminders
- When changing Pydantic models in `prompts.py`, also update the system
  prompt text — they must stay in sync about categories, field meanings,
  intent classification, etc.
- When changing the Google Sheet columns, update `sheets_manager.HEADERS`,
  `_build_row()`, `_get_recent_entries_sync()`, AND `_get_rows_data_sync()`.
- After any architectural change, UPDATE `AGENTS.md`. Add a row to the
  "Recent incidents & learnings" table if you fixed a real-world bug.
- Confidence is based on structured fields only (Date through Amount).
  Description, Notes, and **Category** are best-effort and never lower
  confidence (per explicit user preference — see AGENTS.md "Category
  auto-pick").

## Deployment
- Hosted on **Fly.io** (NOT Railway). See fly.toml and Dockerfile.
- SQLite stored on a persistent volume mounted at `/data`.
- Memory: `512mb` (NEVER revert to 256mb — a single 4MB image will OOM).
- `DB_PATH=/data/bot.db` in Fly.io secrets.
- Logs: `~/.fly/bin/flyctl logs --app musician-expenses-bot`.
